      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "One thing i could drop in here is i have been tweaking my avatar almost every day for a year now, making sure that it's 1:1 tracking for my whole body, including shoulders neck and etc. It was a piece of shit and i find myself still not being satisfied with it at times. But, that happens to fix it in some ways, it almost never occurs and when it does its extremely minor, if i try other avatars then it all goes to shit. people's viewpoint being inside their neck when they are laying down but not when they are standing. And also it seems to happen more often if you use the old way of calibrating. Currently the only way to minimize it is by trying to achieve a more accurate representation of your legs, hips to chest proportions. To minimize the whole compensating that the ik does to make you fit in the avatar. Its a temporary fix. And its hella fun to have 1:1 movement lol, check it out if possible and let me know how it goes.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
